	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Wetlands are a wide country of fen, reed and slow black water that lies north of the mountains of Khaz Modan. Mist hangs over them for much of the year. One great road crosses them: it climbs out of {link:dun-algaz}Dun Algaz{/link} in the south, runs north past the ruins of old dwarven holds, and ends at the {link:thandol-span}Thandol Span{/link}, the bridge that joins the dwarven lands to the human kingdoms of the north. A second road turns west to the sea, where the port of {link:menethil-harbor}Menethil Harbor{/link} keeps the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}'s watch over the coast. It has always been a hard land, rich in crocolisks and raptors and poor in comfort. Now it is also a land at war.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records who first raised stone in these marshes. The dwarves have claimed them for many centuries. In the east stands the mountain fortress of {link:grim-batol}Grim Batol{/link}, once the seat of the Wildhammer clan. In the War of the Three Hammers, the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} struck at Grim Batol, and the dark sorcery unleashed there left the fortress tainted. The Wildhammers abandoned it and went north to the peaks of {link:the-hinterlands}The Hinterlands{/link}. The {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} still finds older things beneath the mud: bones of great beasts, and stones carved in a script that no {link:dwarves}dwarf{/link} wrote.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:menethil-harbor}Menethil Harbor{/link} holds the west coast for the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} under the dwarves of the {link:kingdom-of-ironforge}Kingdom of Ironforge{/link}. Beyond its walls, the Wetlands are coming apart. Dark Iron saboteurs have broken the {link:thandol-span}Thandol Span{/link} and taken {link:dun-modr}Dun Modr{/link}, and the survivors of the regiment that held them wait in the ruins for a reserve that never arrives. The {link:dragonmaw-clan}Dragonmaw orcs{/link}, beaten and scattered after the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, have found a new chieftain and a new camp. They have pushed into {link:dun-algaz}Dun Algaz{/link} and threaten to cut Menethil off from {link:loch-modan}Loch Modan{/link}. At {link:whelgar-s-excavation-site}Whelgar's Excavation Site{/link}, raptors have killed most of an {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} dig. Above that dig, mist has begun to drift down from the mountains, lights flicker on the heights, and constructs of stone walk where no one has walked for ages. The one hopeful news comes by sea: new ships now sail from Menethil to {link:southshore}Southshore{/link} and on to {link:auberdine}Auberdine{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The dwarves of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.{/b} Soldiers, miners, priests and scholars hold {link:menethil-harbor}Menethil Harbor{/link}, the camp outside {link:dun-modr}Dun Modr{/link} and the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} dig.
• {b}The people of Menethil.{/b} {link:humans}Humans{/link} of the old kingdoms work its docks, taverns and tanneries beside the dwarves.
• {b}The {link:dragonmaw-clan}Dragonmaw clan{/link}.{/b} {link:orcs}Orcs{/link} who once rode red dragons to war, now camped in the hills east of the road.
• {b}The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link}.{/b} Their saboteurs, tunnelers and warlocks hold Dun Modr and {link:direforge-hill}Direforge Hill{/link}.
• {b}The Mosshide gnolls.{/b} A {link:gnolls}gnoll{/link} clan of the fens, grown too many for the land that feeds them.
• {b}The Bluegill murlocs.{/b} {link:murlocs}Murlocs{/link} who raid the coast and the merchant ships that pass it.
• {b}The drowned dead.{/b} Cursed sailors still walk the wrecks of the Lost Fleet on the north-western shore.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Three Hammers.{/b} {link:grim-batol}Grim Batol{/link} fell silent after the war of the three clans, and the Wildhammers left the Wetlands behind.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link}.{/b} The {link:horde}Horde{/link} overran Khaz Modan. The {link:dragonmaw-clan}Dragonmaw clan{/link} made Grim Batol its stronghold, and the orcs built a harbor on the west coast to strike at {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad{/link} from the sea. Red dragons under orcish command burned the {link:third-fleet}Third Fleet{/link} of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link} off these shores.
• {b}Menethil.{/b} Admiral {link:daelin-proudmoore}Daelin Proudmoore{/link} routed the orcs from their harbor, and the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} raised a port of its own on the same ground, named for King {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link}.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Irons{/link} rose in the north, the Dragonmaw returned in the east, and the reserves of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} were sent to fight on other fronts.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Wetlands",
			text = [=[• The crocolisk skins of Menethil's tannery are sold in ports around the world.
• A spirit of the marsh, called the Greenwarden, walks among the crocolisks east of the fork to {link:dun-modr}Dun Modr{/link}. Those who seek it are told they will not come back.
• The Mosshide gnolls burn living trees for warmth, and the Greenwarden has not forgiven them.
• The last survivor of the {link:third-fleet}Third Fleet{/link} says that in his dreams he still hears the moans of his drowned brothers.]=],
		},
	},
})

